Animal performances at the slaughterhouse
Animals from the same cohort were slaughtered in the same commercial slaughterhouse when the pen they belonged to approached an average body weight of 720 kg and corresponding to a target market carcass weight of around 430 kg. This corresponded to 22 animals slaughtered right at the end of the RFI test, mostly those fed the corn diet, and the remaining 26 slaughtered several days thereafter (50 ± 14 d) when they reached the targeted body weight. The number of animals within each cohort slaughtered at each time was completely balanced for the RFI groups. Thus, performances at the slaughterhouse were compared at similar body weight and no corrections were performed for differences in age or fattening length. Weights of hot carcass and visceral fat mass (kidney, pelvic and mesenteric fat together) were recorded for each animal.
